<opt:body xmlns:opt="https://www.openpower.tools/ns/opt">
      <p>A scroll container and skin for a regular light-DOM table. Cells stay ordinary
      th/td markup. By default only the header carries a rule - alignment and spacing
      separate the rows - while a lined attribute restores row rules and a dense
      attribute tightens the padding for long reference tables.</p>
      <h2>Example</h2>
      <opt:table>
        <table>
          <caption>Host firmware stack on a stock Talos II</caption>
          <thead><tr><th>Component</th><th>Role</th><th>Status</th></tr></thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr><td>Hostboot</td><td>Brings up the POWER9 cores and memory</td><td><opt:badge variant="ok">tracked</opt:badge></td></tr>
            <tr><td>Skiboot</td><td>OPAL runtime services</td><td><opt:badge variant="ok">tracked</opt:badge></td></tr>
            <tr><td>Petitboot</td><td>Kernel-based boot loader</td><td><opt:badge variant="info">notes</opt:badge></td></tr>
            <tr><td>OpenBMC</td><td>Board management controller stack</td><td><opt:badge variant="warning">docs stale</opt:badge></td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </opt:table>
      <h2>Dense, lined</h2>
      <opt:table dense="" lined="">
        <table>
          <thead><tr><th>Partition</th><th>Size</th></tr></thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr><td>HBB</td><td>512 KiB</td></tr>
            <tr><td>BOOTKERNFW</td><td>16 MiB</td></tr>
            <tr><td>PAYLOAD</td><td>1 MiB</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </opt:table>
      <h2>Markup</h2>
      <pre>&lt;opt:table dense lined&gt;
  &lt;table&gt;...&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;/opt:table&gt;</pre>

</opt:body>
